        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Per K. Sørensen, Frederick I, William II\n- Organizations: Leipzig University\n- Roles: Tibetologist\n- Topics: Tibetan and Himalayan history, literature, culture\n\nFacts:\n- Leipzig University was founded on December 2, 1409 by Frederick I, Elector of Saxony, and his brother William II, Margrave of Meissen.\n- Leipzig University originally comprised the four scholastic faculties.\n- Per Kjeld Sørensen was born on 18 December 1950.\n- Per Kjeld Sørensen is a prominent Danish Tibetologist.\n- Per Kjeld Sørensen specialises in Tibetan and Himalayan history, literature, and culture.",
